  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A sprawling refuge camp built into the skeletal remains of aurora spires that survived the Calving — the catastrophic fracturing of the Frost Zenith's upper shelves triggered by thermal ruptures in the Berg's volcanic core. What remains are the lower thirds of those spires, their crystalline lattices dark and inert, repurposed into wind-breaks and shelter-frames. The aurora-light that once defined this site is gone. Everyone calls it the Waystation now, because *Frost Zenith* died with the spires that gave it meaning.
    
    The Icebound Exchange, the Aurora Stack's nominal governing body, built the original infrastructure. Aureate, the merchant guild that rose from the Still Pools during the Clever Ice Age, administers it now under the terms of the Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith — a treaty between Aureate and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order ratified here, in a converted crystal-vault, by fire-core light because the aurora would not hold. Aureate's people run ration-counts. They are not cruel, just tired.
    
    Migrants shelter here before moving deeper into the Berg or risking the frozen sea. They sleep in carved alcoves originally meant for prayer. The Icebound Exchange's sigil remains visible beneath graffiti — initials of those who did not survive the next winter, bone-token offerings left in cracks no one removes. A memorial wall in the eastern alcove, formally unregulated under the Accord, accumulates names regardless.
    
    ## Deterioration
    
    Corruption bleeds into the lower spires from the Glow-Fissure, one of the Berg's active breach-points. Wild aurora-frost has been observed climbing the trade-spires unbidden — logged in merchant records as crystal discoloration consistent with deep-vein leaching. The diary of one trade-worker documents an uncontrolled crystal bloom at the Zenith and the creeping infection of those exposed. Orca raiders have begun penetrating corridors formerly secured by fire-keeper patrols the ☽'shadow Covens' Order can no longer staff.
    
    The Frost Zenith trades with Dawn Naong, the Beacon Stack, and the Fissured Smelt~. Whether those routes will survive its current decline is not addressed in any source I have seen.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
